WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.399
Everybody knows Deadpool has a mutant healing
factor.

00:00:03.399 --> 00:00:04.690
That's kind of his thing.

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:08.040
It's no secret that he's aware he's a fictional
character, either — breaking the fourth

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.999
wall is what set Deadpool apart from all those
other grizzled, bulky, pouch-wearing '90s

00:00:11.999 --> 00:00:15.589
tough guys, and made him into the wise-cracking
antihero he is today.

00:00:15.589 --> 00:00:18.920
But the Marvel Universe is lousy with mutants
that can heal themselves — besides Deadpool

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:23.880
there's Wolverine, Sabretooth, Mystique, and
X-23, just to name a few — and Wade Wilson

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.860
needed more if he was ever going to get ahead.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.339
Thankfully, Deadpool has plenty of other tricks
up his sleeve.

00:00:30.339 --> 00:00:31.630
Here are a few.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:33.440
Master of disguise

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.719
Deadpool is tough, funny, and charming, but
let's face it: he's not exactly a looker.

00:00:37.719 --> 00:00:42.039
The experimental surgery that gave Wade Wilson
his regenerative powers also kicked his cancer

00:00:42.039 --> 00:00:43.199
into overdrive.

00:00:43.199 --> 00:00:46.710
And while the procedure kept tumors from ravaging
his body, it didn't keep them from growing

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:47.989
all over his face.

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:50.140
As a result, Deadpool looks like, well...

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:51.910
"Like a testicle with teeth."

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:53.270
His words, not ours.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:56.789
Anyway, he understandably prefers not to show
his face in public.

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:58.899
So when he's on the job, that isn't much of
a problem.

00:00:58.899 --> 00:01:02.070
Put a mask over that gruesome mug and nobody
can tell the difference.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.480
But, to hit the town, he has to get creative.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:08.770
In the comics, Deadpool uses a holographic
image inducer and disguises to change his

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:11.330
appearance and wander around incognito.

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:15.890
Deadpool also employs the Teenage Mutant Ninja
Turtles' proven, low-tech disguise: a hat,

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:19.310
a trenchcoat, and the comforting knowledge
that in New York City, a tumor-infested weirdo

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:23.080
probably won't be the weirdest thing you'll
see wandering the streets.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:24.260
Teleportation

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:26.490
Deadpool can't fly, and doesn't have super
speed.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:30.150
So, what's a busy mercenary to do when he
has to get somewhere in a hurry?

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.090
In the movie, he takes a taxi.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:36.430
But that doesn't make for very exciting comics
and, as the film version of Deadpool proved,

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:39.040
Wade's not always great at keeping track of
his belongings.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:40.870
Yep, the guns were in that taxi.

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:44.660
As a result, Deadpool has used a number of
teleportation devices to get around quickly

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:45.740
in the comics.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:49.190
In the early issues of Deadpool, he has a
device tucked away in one of his many pouches

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:51.360
which allows him to zip around with ease.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.710
Then, he even biologically combined with Cable
for a while in the Cable &amp; Deadpool series

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:59.970
due to a crazy virus, which allowed him to
share Cable’s teleportation tech.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.860
Hard to get drunk

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.360
Deadpool's healing factor is pretty handy.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:04.390
It stops cancer.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.390
It cures decapitation.

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:09.450
It lets him walk away from fights with creatures
like the Hulk, and it kicks his metabolism

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.599
into overdrive.

00:02:10.599 --> 00:02:14.040
That's right: no matter how much he eats,
Deadpool won't gain any weight.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.709
That's all good news when you're fighting
supervillains, but isn't so useful when you

00:02:16.709 --> 00:02:20.569
want to get absolutely hammered — and, let's
face it, Wade is the kind of guy who could

00:02:20.569 --> 00:02:22.329
use a drink every now and then.

00:02:22.329 --> 00:02:23.719
But, Deadpool can get drunk.

00:02:23.719 --> 00:02:25.269
He just needs a lot of alcohol to make it
happen.

00:02:25.269 --> 00:02:29.959
In Deadpool #12, Wade spends an entire day
and night drinking before he's even slightly

00:02:29.959 --> 00:02:30.959
buzzed.

00:02:30.959 --> 00:02:34.659
In Deadpool #7, a villain pays Deadpool to
make Iron Man drunk, but instead of forcing

00:02:34.659 --> 00:02:38.239
Tony Stark off the wagon, Deadpool takes care
of business himself.

00:02:38.239 --> 00:02:41.900
Wade clocks Stark with a liquor bottle and
straps into the Iron Man armor, but not before

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:44.269
downing an entire sack full of stolen booze.

00:02:44.269 --> 00:02:48.549
That fulfills Wade's contract — Iron Man
had to get plastered, not Tony — and best

00:02:48.549 --> 00:02:51.329
of all, Deadpool doesn't even have a hangover
when he wakes up.

00:02:51.329 --> 00:02:53.540
Now that's a superpower.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:54.540
Superhuman strength

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:59.260
Deadpool is able to lift between 800 to 50,000
pounds, but you wouldn't know it just by looking

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.260
at him.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:03.370
While super-strength is one of Deadpool's
many powers, you rarely see him lifting heavy

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:06.989
objects, and the only time Wade seems to make
use of his enhanced abilities is when he goes

00:03:06.989 --> 00:03:10.049
toe-to-toe with heavyweights like the Hulk
and the Juggernaut.

00:03:10.049 --> 00:03:13.650
Still, every once in awhile, somebody hints
that Deadpool is a lot stronger than he seems.

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:17.590
During his earliest appearances, he went toe-to-toe
with some of Marvel's strongest characters.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:22.510
In X-Force #11, Shatterstar, a warrior from
the Mojoverse with super-strength, calls Deadpool

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:25.489
his equal — right before Deadpool knocks
him out cold.

00:03:25.489 --> 00:03:30.200
In X-Force #15, Wade is powerful enough to
kick Cable's head through a stone wall.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:33.620
Deadpool's super-strength is made abundantly
clear in Cable &amp; Deadpool #13.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:38.170
Haji Bin Barat, one of the world's most deadly
terrorists, is murdered, and Deadpool wants

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:39.430
to solve the case.

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:43.310
As Deadpool gathers clues, the medical examiner
concludes that Barat was choked by an adult

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:44.910
male using just two fingers.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:49.180
In fact, the murderer actually squeezed too
hard, accidentally snapping Barat's neck mid-killing,

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:51.959
a feat that would require superhuman strength.

00:03:51.959 --> 00:03:55.920
At the same time, Deadpool discovers that
he's the murderer—he just can't immediately

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.420
remember why he did it.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.870
Because, you know, comics.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:00.870
Cursed to be immortal

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:05.810
Thanos, one of the biggest bads in a galaxy
full of big bads, has the hots for Death — as

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:09.810
in, the literal personification of mortality
— and he'll do practically anything to prove

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:10.810
it.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:14.389
So, as you can imagine, Thanos isn't exactly
thrilled when Death and Deadpool strike up

00:04:14.389 --> 00:04:15.389
a relationship.

00:04:15.389 --> 00:04:20.150
In Deadpool/Death Annual '98, Wade first meets
Thanos' would-be gal pal when he's stuck in

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:23.671
the Department K medical facility, undergoing
the treatments that will eventually turn him

00:04:23.671 --> 00:04:24.671
into Deadpool.

00:04:24.671 --> 00:04:28.790
Thanks to his cancer and the government's
experiments, Wade is very, very close to dying,

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:32.490
and Death uses her feminine wiles to try and
convince Wade to finish the job.

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:37.210
However, Wade's newfound healing powers—and
a reluctant sense of heroism—foil his best

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:40.680
attempts at suicide-by-supervillain, and the
couple is forced apart.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:44.670
Later, to keep Deadpool away from Death, Thanos
puts a curse on Wade that brings him back

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:47.840
to life whenever he dies—and will keep him
that way.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.230
Resistant to psychic attacks

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:52.520
Wade’s inability to die isn’t his real
superpower.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:53.860
His insanity is.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:57.410
Deadpool knows he's a comic book character
because he's absolutely crazy, and while his

00:04:57.410 --> 00:05:01.080
broken psyche doesn't help much when it comes
to getting a happy ending, it's a huge boon

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:02.810
when he faces off against psychics.

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:07.150
For example, in Deadpool #69, Deadpool finds
himself in a duel with a telepathic mutant

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:08.680
known as the Black Swan.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:12.440
As they fight, Swan tries to poke around in
Wade's head to find the disarm code for a

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:13.990
bomb Deadpool brought with him.

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:17.680
Unfortunately for Swan, things don't work
exactly like he expected.

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:21.230
Wade welcomes Swan into his mind, which is
a savagely insane place.

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:25.280
That distracts Swan long enough for Deadpool
to shove the villain's head in the fireplace.

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:26.970
Deadpool attempts to defuse the bomb.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.100
But it goes off anyway.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:31.050
Because, hey, Deadpool’s not great with
details.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:33.320
Deadpool's healing powers help fight against
telepathy, too.

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:37.550
In Cable &amp; Deadpool #8, the X-Men enlist Deadpool
to help stop Cable, who's trying to create

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:41.200
peace by uniting the world's nations against
a common enemy—himself.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:45.950
Emma Frost, a psychic, uses Cerebro to shield
the X-Men from Cable's telepathy, but Deadpool

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:49.410
has an easier way: they could've just had
the conversation inside his brain, which is

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:52.760
immune to telepathy thanks to its ever-changing
biology.

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:53.760
Thanks for watching!

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:55.850
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:57.650
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love too!

